Z||000000||Joe Torma||08-25-2001||12:50 PM||||Ok, say you were going to totally redo your dashboard, and where the map pocket was, you decide a 12 Disc CD changer would be nice.  Would you make a glovebox door hiding it-- or leave it exposed, sunk into the dash a little painted to match the interior colors?<P>Thanks,<BR>Joe<P>||||reg||10
Z||000001||Songman||08-25-2001||04:57 PM||||Since I am in the process of putting a passenger side window in one of my Fieros that was broken into I would definitely say hide it..<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||08-25-2001||05:13 PM||||Yeah, that's kinda what I was thinking, but then again, I'll be having a 10.4" LCD Monitor in my dash...can't hide that easily.<P>I do have an alarm system that notifies me of what's going on via pager.<P>I dunno...||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||08-25-2001||05:29 PM||||I almost went that route with a Sony 10 disc changer.  I planned to sink it into the space and make a cover which fastened with velcro for easy access.<P>Instead I got an Xplode CD/MP3 unit so now I can cram some bigger speakers up front instead  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Gary<BR>86 SE ||||reg||12
Z||000004||85fierogt||08-25-2001||05:42 PM||||duyde keep it exposed i mean i can understand the security issues and i totally agree but i think that if you did it right the exposed cd changer would look awsome, my 2 cents<BR>-brad||||reg||1
Z||000005||Joe Torma||08-25-2001||08:07 PM||||Ok, the dash is now 90% ready for covering.  I decided to sink the changer into it.<P>85, got any suggestions for asthetics?  I have black vinyl, and was going to paint the changer face black, and the door silver.<P>The color scheme of the car is purple(paint), black(most int pieces, moulding), and silver(trim, wheels)<P>Any ideas?<P>||||reg||1
